  "notes": [
    "Regular -AR verb — follows standard -AR endings with no exceptions",
    "Past participle: *regresado* (regular)",
    "Means \"to return\" or \"to come/go back\" — *regresó a casa tarde* (he/she came home late), *regresaremos el lunes* (we'll be back on Monday)",
    "Very common in Latin American Spanish as the everyday equivalent of *volver*; both are used, but *regresar* is often preferred outside Spain",
    "Related: *regreso* (return, noun — *de regreso a casa* = on the way back home)"
  ],
